#: src/listing-available-recipes.md:1
msgid "Listing Available Recipes"
msgstr ""

#: src/listing-available-recipes.md:3
msgid "Recipes can be listed in alphabetical order with `just --list`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/listing-available-recipes.md:14
msgid ""
"Recipes in [submodules](modules.html) can be listed with `just --list PATH`, "
"where `PATH` is a space- or `::`\\-separated module path:"
msgstr ""

#: src/listing-available-recipes.md:32
msgid "`just --summary` is more concise:"
msgstr ""

#: src/listing-available-recipes.md:39
msgid ""
"Pass `--unsorted` to print recipes in the order they appear in the "
"`justfile`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/listing-available-recipes.md:61
msgid ""
"If you’d like `just` to default to listing the recipes in the `justfile`, "
"set `default-list`<sup>1.52.0</sup>:"
msgstr ""

#: src/listing-available-recipes.md:68
msgid ""
"The setting is per-module, so invoking a module path with `default-list` "
"enabled lists that module’s recipes."
msgstr ""

#: src/listing-available-recipes.md:71
msgid ""
"You can also default to listing recipes this behavior by settting the "
"environment variable `JUST_DEFAULT_LIST=true` or passing `--default-"
"list`<sup>1.52.0</sup>."
msgstr ""

#: src/listing-available-recipes.md:75
msgid "The heading text can be customized with `--list-heading`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/listing-available-recipes.md:84
msgid "And the indentation can be customized with `--list-prefix`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/listing-available-recipes.md:93
msgid ""
"The argument to `--list-heading` replaces both the heading and the newline "
"following it, so it should contain a newline if non-empty. It works this way "
